---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import DockerEnvGenerator from '../../components/DockerEnvGenerator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Docker Environment File Generator" description="Generate a .env file and matching docker-compose environment reference from a simple variable list.">
  <DockerEnvGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why separate .env from docker-compose.yml</h2>
  <p>Keeping environment values in a separate .env file (rather than hardcoded in docker-compose.yml) lets you swap configuration between environments without editing the compose file itself, and keeps secrets out of a file you might commit to version control.</p>

  <h2>How to use this generator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>List your variable names and values.</li>
    <li>Copy the generated .env file content.</li>
    <li>Reference the variables in your docker-compose.yml using the generated syntax.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common Docker .env Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Committing a real .env file to version control</strong> — add it to .gitignore and commit only an .env.example template with placeholder values.</li>
    <li><strong>Forgetting docker-compose needs the .env file in the same directory</strong> as the compose file to be picked up automatically by default.</li>
    <li><strong>Mixing build-time and runtime variables</strong> without understanding that some need to be passed as build args, not just environment variables.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Docker Env Generator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Setting up environment-specific configuration for a Dockerized app</li>
    <li>Providing a clean .env.example template for new developers</li>
    <li>Separating secrets from a docker-compose.yml file destined for version control</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Docker Environment File FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does .env work with plain docker run too?</strong> The .env file format itself is simple key-value pairs; docker-compose reads it automatically, while plain <code>docker run</code> needs the <code>--env-file</code> flag to use it.</p>
</ToolLayout>
